we Europeans suffer from the greatest  human tragedy since the wars we are all  heartbroken by the death of many  thousands of people killed by the  coronavirus the first and hardest hit  are Italy in Spain and we are mourning  with them our daily life has changed  dramatically  millions of people cannot go to work but  they still have to buy groceries and pay  the bills companies are paying salaries  to their employees even if right now  they are not making money Europe is now  coming to their support with a new  initiative it is called sure for example  the regions around mulana or Madrid they  are part of the backbone of Europe's  economy thousands of strong and healthy  companies are struggling because of the  current crisis they need our support to  get through the crisis and this is why  we have developed a concept of short  time work it is intended to help Italy  Spain and all other countries that have  been hearted and it will do so thanks to  the Solidarity of other Member States  how does sure work we have learned the  lessons from the financial crisis in  2008 Member States who had this  instrument helped millions of people to  stay in their jobs and companies to go  through the financial crisis with their  employees this is sure state-supported  short-time work it has mitigated the  effects of the recession kept people in  work and enabled companies to return to  the markets with renewed vigor and the  idea is simple if there are no orders  and companies run out of work because of  a temporary external shock like aronia  they should not lay off their workers  they continue to employ them even if  there's less work in the spare time  workers might be taught for example news  skills that will benefit both the  company and themselves this way people  are spared the hole in their wallets  during the crisis they can continue to  pay the rents and buy what they need and  this also has a positive impact on the  economy thanks to sure more people will  keep their job during the corona crisis  and they will go back to full work as  soon as the lockdown will be over when  the demand picks up again and the orders  come back this is crucial to restart  Europe's economic engine without delay  this week the European Commission will  propose a new instrument to support  short time work it will help in the  countries the most hit and it is  guaranteed by all Member States this is  European solidarity in action it is for  Italy Spain and others and it is for  Europe's future
 

